RuntimeError: Newton reported a contact-buffer overflow at num_envs=32 during the rollout (step 325) (6 warnings). Contacts are being dropped and every number from this run would be measured on a scene where the hand cannot fully feel the object.

  nefc overflow - please increase njmax to 8525
  nefc overflow - please increase njmax to 9596
  nefc overflow - please increase njmax to 13330
  nefc overflow - please increase njmax to 10219
  nefc overflow - please increase njmax to 12522
  nefc overflow - please increase njmax to 8274

Buffer budgets in Newton are GLOBAL, not per-env, so they must scale with num_envs AND with scene geometry -- a 24-segment cable generates far more triangle pairs than a 12-segment one at the same env count. Check that the sized budget reaches the solver: a coupled scene builds a separate CollisionPipeline per proxy, and that one defaults to max_triangle_pairs=1e6 regardless of NewtonCfg.collision_cfg.
